;; One mutation per invariant. `:find` must occur EXACTLY ONCE in `:file` —
;; `tools/mutate.cljk` refuses otherwise, because a mutation that landed in a
;; comment or a second call site produces a red suite that proves nothing.
;;
;; ## SCOPE
;;
;; Covers the 2026-08-18 `.clj` → `.cljc` conversion: that the registry is
;; compiled in rather than read at runtime, that the generated projection
;; cannot drift from the EDN unnoticed, and that a registry handed in as nil
;; does not flatten into a complete-looking empty lookup. Two mutations reach
;; slightly further, into the backlog partition and the maturity default,
;; because both are answers a caller cannot distinguish from "the registry
;; was empty" and that is the same class of defect. It does NOT cover
;; readiness, execution-plan shape, the wave assignment, or the ~400
;; per-actor `*-is-implemented` assertions — those have 1,826 assertions and
;; no mutations here, so a clean run of this table means "the portability
;; invariants are measured" and NOT "this library is measured".
;;
;; ⚠ These mutations drive `kbb -M:test`. The `:cljs` half is exercised
;; by `test/run_portable.cljk`, which this harness does not run — a mutation
;; that broke only a `:cljs` branch would survive here. Both were run by
;; hand; see the conversion commit message for the counts.
;;
;; ## What a blind run found
;;
;; The table was written before looking at the suite. Two entries SURVIVED
;; the whole 1,826-assertion suite, and both were real gaps:
;;
;;   :the-backlog-partitions-required-from-optional — nothing distinguished
;;   the `:required` half of `unprovided-technologies` from the `:optional`
;;   half. The existing cases could not: 4210 pins only `:required`, and 7911
;;   has both empty. An unprovided OPTIONAL technology reported as required
;;   turns a nice-to-have into something that looks like it blocks a launch.
;;   Closed by `the-backlog-tells-required-apart-from-optional`.
;;
;;   :maturity-defaults-to-spec — every live registry entry carries an
;;   explicit `:maturity`, so `(or (:maturity entry) …)` short-circuits and
;;   the `cond` beneath it was dead code as far as the suite could see, which
;;   is exactly the situation `maturity-of`'s own docstring anticipated.
;;   Closed by `maturity-defaults-to-spec-when-the-entry-claims-nothing`.
;;
;; Both are recorded rather than quietly fixed: a table that only ever shows
;; kills is not evidence that anything was written blind.
;;
;; NOT written, with the reason: replacing `([] (industries (registry)))`
;; with `([] (:industries (registry)))`. It is a semantic no-op — the one-arg
;; body IS `(:industries reg)` — so it reddens nothing for every input
;; including nil. The single-path form is still worth having (a guard added
;; to the one-arg form cannot be skipped by the zero-arg one) but it is not
;; an invariant anything can observe today. The same no-op was written and
;; removed in `kotoba-lang/technology` and `kotoba-lang/iso3166`.
[{:id :the-projection-cannot-drift-unnoticed
  :invariant "the generated namespace matches the EDN a human edits"
  :file "src/kotoba/industry/embedded.cljk"
  :find "Community Monetary Intermediation"
  :replace "Community Monetary Intermediation DRIFTED"}

 {:id :the-drift-check-refuses-when-it-cannot-read
  :invariant "a check that could not run must not report a pass"
  :file "test/kotoba/industry_test.cljk"
  :find "#?(:clj (try (slurp path) (catch Exception _ nil))"
  :replace "#?(:clj (try (slurp (str path \".missing\")) (catch Exception _ nil))"}

 {:id :by-id-does-not-invent-an-empty-index
  :invariant "(into {} …) over nil yields {} — an index over no data"
  :file "src/kotoba/industry.cljk"
  :find "  ([reg] (when-let [inds (industries reg)]\n           (into {} (map (juxt :id identity)) inds))))"
  :replace "  ([reg] (into {} (map (juxt :id identity)) (industries reg))))"}

 {:id :by-id-is-keyed-on-the-isic-class
  :invariant "the index key is :id and not some other field"
  :file "src/kotoba/industry.cljk"
  :find "(map (juxt :id identity)) inds)"
  :replace "(map (juxt :name identity)) inds)"}

 ;; ⚠ RETARGETED, with the reason. The first form of this mutation replaced
 ;; `embedded/registry-data` with `{}`. It is caught — run by hand it gives
 ;; `Ran 50 tests containing 519 assertions. 434 failures` — but the HARNESS
 ;; cannot score it: `tools/mutate.cljk` runs `kbb -M:test` under Node's
 ;; `execSync`, whose default `maxBuffer` is 1 MB, and 434 clojure.test
 ;; failure reports exceed that. Node then kills the child with SIGTERM, and
 ;; the harness — correctly, given what it can see — treats a signalled child
 ;; as an interrupted run, restores the file and exits 143 without scoring
 ;; anything. So on a suite this large a mutation must redden a BOUNDED
 ;; number of tests to be scoreable at all. This one is narrowed to altering
 ;; the projection rather than replacing it; the broad version's result is
 ;; recorded above instead of being silently dropped.
 {:id :the-registry-is-the-projection-unaltered
  :invariant "the library returns the projection as it is, not a doctored copy"
  :file "src/kotoba/industry.cljk"
  :find "  embedded/registry-data)"
  :replace "  (dissoc embedded/registry-data :kotoba.registry/id))"}

 {:id :the-backlog-partitions-required-from-optional
  :invariant "an unprovided OPTIONAL technology is not reported as required"
  :file "src/kotoba/industry.cljk"
  :find "    :optional (:unknown (technology/resolve-stack (optional-technologies reg isic)))}))"
  :replace "    :optional (:unknown (technology/resolve-stack (required-technologies reg isic)))}))"}

 {:id :maturity-defaults-to-spec
  :invariant "an entry with no evidence of a repo is :spec, not a tier up"
  :file "src/kotoba/industry.cljk"
  :find "        :else                    :spec)))"
  :replace "        :else                    :blueprint)))"}]
